NimbyTapes (Music) - original work by Jeff Fabish for NIMBY | HARDCORE | BADLANDS | 1pp.
A cassette deck, tapes, and a 9V battery, built on the vanilla DayZ 1.30 item, energy-manager,
and action frameworks (Bohemia Interactive). Plan: docs/plans/2026-11-09-music-plan.md (Plan 13).
Own build, no Community Framework (ruling M-1, Jeff, November 9, 2026).

Credit: the playback sync method (the server publishes the elapsed time of the track, and each
client starts its own sound at that offset) follows Zens Music by Zenarchist,
https://github.com/ZenarchistCode/ZenMusic, read at commit 3de1452
(ZenMusicBase/scripts/4_World/ZenMusicBase/Entities/ZenMusic/Devices/Zen_MusicDeviceBase.c:226-227,329-344).
His pack wiki states MPL 2.0 for all his mods; the ZenMusic repository carries no licence file,
and its readme permits repacking. The stub below holds none of his code. When the Phase 0 body
lands, this file lists every method or file taken, with its source file, commit, and licence,
as the Hands and Legs forks do.

No audio ships in this addon on main: the Phase 0 timing tracks are generated locally into
sound\ and are git-ignored (plan P4).

